{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0098f537af91e14235dadc780e9896970d1fdc0d3a78534c87711bd95833c5d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states MCP tools must pass three independent checks before use - registry whitelist, a per-service enable toggle, and credential availability - and that of the preset MCP services, thirteen lower-frequency or higher-risk ones default to disabled while a smaller default-enabled set covers web search, maps, and image/video generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0ae4a2b69195d13ba20965d3d65e1ce101d0141c47f552bec729041418db2cf0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes a unified authorization pipeline where core tools pass through a Tool Gateway: input normalization, an Operation Analyzer risk/resource check, a system-invariant check, a RUN/SESSION/WORKSPACE grant match or persistent-permission prompt, a pre-execution recheck, and a structured audit of results; high-risk operations are limited to single-use authorization."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e69d18a33e2cdd269485b7c25ae19c899962346c4cd50571a19124cf2675735"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states that on a 402 quota-exceeded or 404 model-unavailable response, the system automatically cools that key down for 15 minutes and switches to the next configured API key."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4c2cdb1d021845b04961d62fde11c847001644578f7786be91005ea18d076c1b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states Docker deployment ships the Java backend and a built-in static frontend by default in one container, with an optional managed Python service included in the image but not started, and not exposing a port, unless explicitly enabled via environment variables or a compose override."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7977a466349508f09e7091b0507a2e17bbcdbd95b8a97eddd92fa07842ea42e6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes a three-tier architecture: a Java 21/Spring Boot backend handling core orchestration, LLM routing, and the authorization gateway; a React/TypeScript frontend for the interactive UI; and an optional Python/FastAPI service for code analysis and MCP bridging."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7a1621f582660cf19c0e826b30472346b732baa66e3e26df82507c75f9bde81c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation states that referencing a local file when connected directly adds only its path to the prompt without uploading content, but doing so over a remote or proxied connection instead uploads the file as a permanent public OSS object and requires OSS to be configured first."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a70e6822e385ce9d3c5eb8b2c4eb30ae29da878f792680000a6bec228c9a9711"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes ZhikunCode as an open-source AI programming assistant deployed once and controllable entirely from a browser, with multi-agent collaboration, Docker self-hosting, direct connections to domestic Chinese LLM providers, and what it calls a deep security architecture."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf1be386b8c04cdab5abe264204053ccdc0b441eafeab0e42fb591740c28da0c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes a six-level context-compression cascade (Snip, MicroCompact, ContextCollapse, AutoCompact, CollapseDrain, ReactiveCompact) intended to keep sessions within the context window, with a documented two-stage CollapseDrain/ReactiveCompact recovery path for large sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e7e501fd2cdf4edbfe1ee3f688e49ebd796e05d2c59bd3a3b60320143e8732b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README lists three multi-agent collaboration modes: Team for fixed role division, Swarm for dynamic negotiation, and SubAgent for master/subordinate delegation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f3b98eebe4bd0845a84c2740ed886384d63b8e37cd795aa140037cf7d63174f2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports ZhikunCode completed the SWE-bench Lite benchmark (300 instances, pass@1) against an official harness, with a resolve rate of 168/300 (56.0%) and a patch-generation rate of 284/300 (94.7%), and states the evaluation artifacts are open-sourced for third-party reproduction."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f84a0ca9b1f834a385ec9ce087d194537dd0511f1fc07ceb23772700fd4c96c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A documented provider table lists direct connections to DashScope (Qianwen, the default), DeepSeek, Moonshot (Kimi), Zhipu GLM, and MiniMax as domestic options, plus OpenAI (requiring external network access) and a fully offline local Ollama option."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0098f537af91e14235dadc780e9896970d1fdc0d3a78534c87711bd95833c5d3","clm_0ae4a2b69195d13ba20965d3d65e1ce101d0141c47f552bec729041418db2cf0","clm_0e69d18a33e2cdd269485b7c25ae19c899962346c4cd50571a19124cf2675735","clm_4c2cdb1d021845b04961d62fde11c847001644578f7786be91005ea18d076c1b","clm_7977a466349508f09e7091b0507a2e17bbcdbd95b8a97eddd92fa07842ea42e6","clm_7a1621f582660cf19c0e826b30472346b732baa66e3e26df82507c75f9bde81c","clm_a70e6822e385ce9d3c5eb8b2c4eb30ae29da878f792680000a6bec228c9a9711","clm_cf1be386b8c04cdab5abe264204053ccdc0b441eafeab0e42fb591740c28da0c","clm_e7e501fd2cdf4edbfe1ee3f688e49ebd796e05d2c59bd3a3b60320143e8732b4","clm_f3b98eebe4bd0845a84c2740ed886384d63b8e37cd795aa140037cf7d63174f2","clm_f84a0ca9b1f834a385ec9ce087d194537dd0511f1fc07ceb23772700fd4c96c6"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","id":"pg_e8a0ef2b0328598796e836d130ac47e5","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhikunqingtao-zhikuncode-readme-md-931a9beebf21-36d130ac47e5.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"title":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode/README.md @ 931a9beebf21","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
